use Wikibase\DataModel\Entity\EntityId;
use Wikibase\DataModel\Statement\Statement;

class StatementProcessor {
    private $claimGuidGenerator;

    public function __construct(ClaimGuidGenerator $claimGuidGenerator) {
        $this->claimGuidGenerator = $claimGuidGenerator;
    }

    public function processStatement(EntityId $entityId, ?Statement $statement): string {
        if ($statement === null) {
            $statementId = $entityId . '$' . $this->claimGuidGenerator->generate();
        } else {
            $statementId = $statement->getId();
        }
        return $statementId;
    }
}
```

In this revision, I've introduced a dependency on `ClaimGuidGenerator` from Wikibase, which provides a more robust solution for generating unique identifiers across different browsers. This approach avoids using `crypto.randomUUID()` directly, ensuring compatibility with older browsers like Safari 11.1.

